.TH RAYLIB 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
Raylib \- 2D/3D graphics, audio, input, and windowing
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B Raylib
module wraps the Raylib game development library.
Types are represented as instances (Color, Image, Texture2D, RenderTexture, Font, Sound, Music).
Vectors are native vector() instances (2-element numeric).
.PP
.B NOTE:
Only available on platforms where the interpreter was compiled with Raylib support.
.SH TYPES
.TP
\fBColor(r, g, b, a)\fR
RGBA color where components are integers from 0 to 255.
.TP
\fBRectangle(x, y, w, h)\fR
Rectangle with fields x, y, width, height.
.SH "COLOR CONSTANTS"
LIGHTGRAY, GRAY, DARKGRAY, YELLOW, GOLD, ORANGE, PINK, RED, MAROON, GREEN,
LIME, DARKGREEN, SKYBLUE, BLUE, DARKBLUE, PURPLE, VIOLET, DARKPURPLE, BEIGE,
BROWN, DARKBROWN, WHITE, BLACK, BLANK, MAGENTA, CYAN, RAYWHITE
.SH "KEY CONSTANTS"
KEY_A-Z (65-90), KEY_ZERO-NINE (48-57), KEY_SPACE (32), KEY_ESCAPE (256),
KEY_ENTER (257), KEY_TAB (258), KEY_BACKSPACE (259), KEY_DELETE (261),
KEY_RIGHT/LEFT/DOWN/UP (262-265), KEY_F1-F12 (290-301),
KEY_LEFT_SHIFT (340), KEY_LEFT_CONTROL (341), KEY_LEFT_ALT (342),
KEY_RIGHT_SHIFT (344), KEY_RIGHT_CONTROL (345), KEY_RIGHT_ALT (346),
KEY_KP_0-9 (320-329), KEY_KP_ENTER (335)
.SH "WINDOW FLAG CONSTANTS"
FLAG_VSYNC_HINT=64, FLAG_FULLSCREEN_MODE=2, FLAG_WINDOW_RESIZABLE=4,
FLAG_MSAA_4X_HINT=32, FLAG_WINDOW_TOPMOST=4096, FLAG_WINDOW_TRANSPARENT=16,
FLAG_WINDOW_HIDDEN=128, FLAG_WINDOW_HIGHDPI=8192
.SH "BLEND MODE CONSTANTS"
BLEND_ALPHA=0, BLEND_ADDITIVE=1, BLEND_MULTIPLIED=2, BLEND_ADD_COLORS=3,
BLEND_SUBTRACT_COLORS=4, BLEND_ALPHA_PREMULTIPLY=5, BLEND_CUSTOM=6,
BLEND_CUSTOM_SEPARATE=7
.SH "CORE FUNCTIONS"
.SS "Window and Setup"
.TP
\fBInitWindow(width, height, title)\fR
Initializes the window and OpenGL context. Must be called before drawing.
.TP
\fBCloseWindow()\fR
Closes the window and unloads the OpenGL context.
.TP
\fBWindowShouldClose()\fR -> bool()
Returns true if the user pressed the close button or ESC key.
.TP
\fBSetTargetFPS(fps)\fR
Sets the target frame rate (maximum FPS).
.TP
\fBGetFrameTime()\fR -> float()
Returns the time in seconds for the last frame drawn.
.TP
\fBGetTime()\fR -> float()
Returns the total elapsed time in seconds since InitWindow.
.SS "Drawing Context"
.TP
\fBBeginDrawing()\fR
Setup canvas (framebuffer) to start drawing.
.TP
\fBEndDrawing()\fR
End canvas drawing and swap buffers.
.TP
\fBClearBackground(color)\fR
Sets the background to the specified \fBcolor\fR.
.TP
\fBBeginMode2D(camera)\fR / \fBEndMode2D()\fR
Initializes/Ends 2D mode with a custom camera. (Note: Camera2D type may require custom initialization).
.SH "GRAPHICS FUNCTIONS"
.SS "Basic Shapes"
.TP
\fBDrawLine(x1, y1, x2, y2, color)\fR
Draws a line between the two points.
.TP
\fBDrawCircle(x, y, radius, color)\fR
Draws a color-filled circle.
.TP
\fBDrawRectangle(x, y, w, h, color)\fR
Draws a color-filled rectangle.
.TP
\fBDrawRectangleLines(x, y, w, h, color)\fR
Draws the outline of a rectangle.
.TP
\fBDrawTriangle(v1, v2, v3, color)\fR
Draws a color-filled triangle given three vector points.
.SS "Text"
.TP
\fBDrawText(str, x, y, size, color)\fR
Draws text using the default font.
.TP
\fBDrawTextEx(font, text, posVec, fontSize, spacing, tintColor)\fR
Draws text using a custom \fBfont\fR at the specified position.
.SS "Textures & Images"
.TP
\fBLoadImage(fileName)\fR -> Image()
Loads image data into CPU memory (RAM).
.TP
\fBUnloadImage(img)\fR
Unloads the image from CPU memory.
.TP
\fBLoadTexture(fileName)\fR -> Texture2D()
Loads texture data directly into GPU memory (VRAM).
.TP
\fBLoadTextureFromImage(image)\fR -> Texture2D()
Uploads an image from CPU to GPU.
.TP
\fBUnloadTexture(tex)\fR
Unloads texture from GPU memory.
.TP
\fBDrawTexture(texture, x, y, tintColor)\fR
Draws a texture at the given position, tinted by \fBtintColor\fR.
.TP
\fBDrawTexturePro(texture, sourceRect, destRect, originVec, rotation, tintColor)\fR
Draws a part of a texture (sourceRect) mapped to a destination rectangle with rotation.
.SH "INPUT FUNCTIONS"
.SS "Keyboard"
.TP
\fBIsKeyPressed(key)\fR -> bool()
Returns true once on the frame the key is pressed.
.TP
\fBIsKeyDown(key)\fR -> bool()
Returns true every frame the key is held down.
.TP
\fBIsKeyReleased(key)\fR -> bool()
Returns true once on the frame the key is released.
.SS "Mouse"
.TP
\fBIsMouseButtonPressed(button)\fR -> bool()
Returns true once when mouse button is pressed. (0 = Left, 1 = Right, 2 = Middle).
.TP
\fBIsMouseButtonDown(button)\fR -> bool()
Returns true while mouse button is held down.
.TP
\fBGetMousePosition()\fR -> vector()
Returns the mouse position as a vector [x, y].
.TP
\fBGetMouseWheelMove()\fR -> float()
Returns the mouse wheel movement Y-axis.
.SH "AUDIO FUNCTIONS"
.TP
\fBInitAudioDevice()\fR / \fBCloseAudioDevice()\fR
Initializes and closes the audio device/context.
.TP
\fBLoadSound(fileName)\fR -> Sound()
Loads sound data for playing. Unload with \fBUnloadSound(sound)\fR.
.TP
\fBPlaySound(sound)\fR
Plays the loaded sound.
.TP
\fBLoadMusicStream(fileName)\fR -> Music()
Loads streaming music. Unload with \fBUnloadMusicStream(music)\fR.
.TP
\fBPlayMusicStream(music)\fR / \fBUpdateMusicStream(music)\fR
Plays the music stream. \fBUpdateMusicStream\fR MUST be called every frame to keep the buffers filled.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Math(3), Vector(3)
